WEBVTT

00:00:00.358 --> 00:00:05.180
Chapter 1 Going nowhere.

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:10.554
Huminda looked at her watch and then at the traffic outside.

00:00:10.614 --> 00:00:16.826
The airport was 10km away and it was already 5.15pm.

00:00:16.886 --> 00:00:21.069
Isn't there a quicker way to get to the airport?

00:00:21.129 --> 00:00:24.501
My plane leaves in less than 2 hours.

00:00:24.561 --> 00:00:27.081
She asked the taxi driver.

00:00:27.141 --> 00:00:29.791
Are you going home for Christmas?"

00:00:29.851 --> 00:00:31.122
he smiled.

00:00:31.182 --> 00:00:34.323
The taxi was full of decorations.

00:00:34.383 --> 00:00:40.415
There was green tinsel on the steering wheel and mistletoe under the mirror.

00:00:40.475 --> 00:00:43.126
Yes, said Haminda.

00:00:43.186 --> 00:00:47.198
But there was no Christmas spirit in her voice.

00:00:47.258 --> 00:00:52.200
Haminda looked out of the window, trying not to cry.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:57.010
She remembered the phone call from her mum earlier that day.

00:00:57.070 --> 00:01:00.070
She missed her parents so much.

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:05.213
Their argument, four years ago, seemed stupid now.

00:01:05.273 --> 00:01:09.806
Thirty minutes later, they arrived at Galway Airport.

00:01:09.866 --> 00:01:11.627
How much is it?

00:01:11.687 --> 00:01:13.919
She asked.

00:01:13.979 --> 00:01:16.230
15 euros for you, sweetheart.

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:19.332
Said the taxi driver with a smile.

00:01:19.392 --> 00:01:25.308
Haminda gave him a 20 euro note and got quickly out of the taxi.

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:27.400
Don't forget your change!"

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:32.264
shouted the taxi driver, with a five-year-old note in his hand.

00:01:32.324 --> 00:01:37.108
But Haminda was already inside the airport terminal.

00:01:37.168 --> 00:01:45.395
There were a lot of people, and Haminda pushed through the crowd to look at the screens for her flight.

00:01:45.455 --> 00:01:47.456
Cancelled.

00:01:47.516 --> 00:01:51.901
Stay calm and read it again, slowly.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.272
You've read it wrong, that's all.

00:01:54.332 --> 00:01:59.014
She thought.

00:01:59.074 --> 00:02:11.843
All flights from Galway were cancelled because of bad weather.

00:02:11.903 --> 00:02:17.268
I'm sorry, but tomorrow's flight to London is fully booked.

00:02:17.328 --> 00:02:20.666
Christmas is a busy time of year.

00:02:20.726 --> 00:02:27.015
said the man at the ticket office when Haminda tried to find another flight.

00:02:27.075 --> 00:02:29.856
What about another airport?

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:31.516
Dublin perhaps?

00:02:31.576 --> 00:02:32.537
Sorry.

00:02:32.597 --> 00:02:34.848
You don't understand.

00:02:34.908 --> 00:02:36.408
Said Haminda.

00:02:36.468 --> 00:02:40.300
I have to get to London as soon as possible.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.380
My dad's ill.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:45.532
I really am very sorry.

00:02:45.592 --> 00:02:48.282
The man said sympathetically.

00:02:48.342 --> 00:02:50.608
You could hire a car.

00:02:50.668 --> 00:02:56.246
It's a long journey, but if you need to get there quickly."

00:02:56.306 --> 00:03:06.486
As Harmina ran towards Karhaya, she saw that there were only two women waiting, and she started to feel hopeful.

00:03:06.546 --> 00:03:09.608
I'm sorry, but this is the last car.

00:03:09.668 --> 00:03:11.711
She heard the assistant say.

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:14.042
But I was here first.

00:03:14.102 --> 00:03:16.906
Shouted a tall, blonde woman.

00:03:16.966 --> 00:03:23.219
Only because you pushed in front of me, I'm getting married in three days, I have to get to London.

00:03:23.279 --> 00:03:26.940
Shouted an Irish girl in her late 20s.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:30.542
And I've got a very important audition.

00:03:30.602 --> 00:03:32.452
Said the blonde woman.

00:03:32.512 --> 00:03:34.013
Excuse me.

00:03:34.073 --> 00:03:35.823
Interrupted, Arminda.

00:03:35.883 --> 00:03:38.854
Did you say that there's only one car?

00:03:38.914 --> 00:03:40.955
Yes, and it's mine.

00:03:41.015 --> 00:03:43.116
Said the blonde, arrogantly.

00:03:43.176 --> 00:03:44.596
No, it's not.

00:03:44.656 --> 00:03:46.971
The argument continued.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:52.757
Haminda wanted to cry, but then she had an idea.

00:03:52.816 --> 00:03:57.689
If you two are going to London, we can share the car.

00:03:57.749 --> 00:03:59.290
What do you think?

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:02.642
We can share the driving and the cost.

00:04:02.701 --> 00:04:06.683
The two women looked at her in silence.

00:04:06.743 --> 00:04:09.334
They probably think I'm mad.

00:04:09.394 --> 00:04:10.877
Thought Haminda.

00:04:10.937 --> 00:04:13.221
But that didn't worry her.

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:18.954
The only thing that worried her was getting to London to see her family.

00:04:19.014 --> 00:04:23.298
Well, if you want to get to your audition.

00:04:23.357 --> 00:04:25.849
Huminda said to the blonde.

00:04:25.909 --> 00:04:28.982
And if you want to get married.

00:04:29.042 --> 00:04:31.363
She said to the other woman.

00:04:31.423 --> 00:04:34.549
Well, you've got no choice.

00:04:34.609 --> 00:04:41.928
Haminda was speaking angrily, and after a moment the two women reluctantly agreed.

00:04:41.988 --> 00:04:44.510
Mr. O'Flahty will be pleased.

00:04:44.569 --> 00:04:50.304
Thought Chrissie, the car hire assistant, as she showed the women their car.

00:04:50.364 --> 00:04:51.944
Chrissie!

00:04:52.004 --> 00:04:52.915
Chrissie!

00:04:52.975 --> 00:04:56.128
A man shouted, running towards them.

00:04:56.188 --> 00:05:02.844
It was very cold, but he was sweating, and his face was red and angry.

00:05:02.903 --> 00:05:04.596
Oh, that's my boss.

00:05:04.656 --> 00:05:05.926
Merry Christmas!

00:05:05.986 --> 00:05:08.738
She smiled and closed the door.

00:05:08.798 --> 00:05:10.859
Stop them, Chrissy!

00:05:10.919 --> 00:05:12.030
What?

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:14.191
It's okay, Mr. O'Flahati.

00:05:14.251 --> 00:05:15.231
They've peed?

00:05:15.291 --> 00:05:19.244
She smiled, waving at the car as it left.

00:05:19.304 --> 00:05:23.035
That car was reserved, you stupid girl.

00:05:23.095 --> 00:05:24.426
He shouted.

00:05:24.486 --> 00:05:27.067
Chrissy's face turned red.

00:05:27.127 --> 00:05:32.748
She didn't see the three businessmen as she ran into the airport, crying.

00:05:32.808 --> 00:05:36.038
Where is my car, Mr. O'Flahati?"

00:05:36.098 --> 00:05:37.429
asked one.

00:05:37.488 --> 00:05:43.083
His voice was calm, but his grey eyes were dangerous.

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:52.508
Colin O'Flahati turned around nervously to talk to the three men, and he knew that he was in trouble.

00:05:52.568 --> 00:05:56.202
Big trouble.

00:05:56.261 --> 00:06:05.131
Chapter 2 Galway to Dublin Don't worry.

00:06:05.151 --> 00:06:06.311
I'll be there.

00:06:06.331 --> 00:06:08.242
I love you too."

00:06:08.302 --> 00:06:10.992
said Shauna, the Irish girl.

00:06:11.052 --> 00:06:13.243
She was on the phone.

00:06:13.303 --> 00:06:15.724
Was that your fiancé?

00:06:15.783 --> 00:06:19.264
asked Haminde when Shauna finished speaking.

00:06:19.324 --> 00:06:20.465
Yes.

00:06:20.525 --> 00:06:22.895
She replied with a smile.

00:06:22.955 --> 00:06:26.604
And you're getting married on Christmas Eve?

00:06:26.664 --> 00:06:28.684
So romantic.

00:06:28.744 --> 00:06:29.854
I know.

00:06:29.914 --> 00:06:31.526
Graham is romantic.

00:06:31.585 --> 00:06:32.626
She said.

00:06:32.686 --> 00:06:37.170
She took a photo from her purse and gave it to Huminda.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:40.942
It was obvious that she loved him very much.

00:06:41.002 --> 00:06:44.035
He even proposed on Valentine's Day.

00:06:44.095 --> 00:06:45.516
Original.

00:06:45.576 --> 00:06:47.858
Said Vanessa, sarcastically.

00:06:47.918 --> 00:06:49.419
What is your problem?

00:06:49.479 --> 00:06:54.708
Replied Shauna, angry at the blonde woman's sarcastic reply.

00:06:54.768 --> 00:06:57.155
I'm not the one with the problem.

00:06:57.214 --> 00:06:59.176
I'm not the one getting married.

00:06:59.236 --> 00:07:00.337
Thank God.

00:07:00.397 --> 00:07:08.143
We left Galway two hours ago, and the only thing you've talked about is Gavin and how wonderful he is.

00:07:08.203 --> 00:07:09.854
His name's Graham.

00:07:09.914 --> 00:07:12.386
Graham, Gavin, whatever.

00:07:12.446 --> 00:07:14.138
So he's romantic?

00:07:14.198 --> 00:07:21.044
After six months of marriage it won't be romantic when you have to wash his dirty clothes every week.

00:07:21.104 --> 00:07:24.547
Vanessa, that's a horrible thing to say.

00:07:24.607 --> 00:07:26.048
Said Haminda.

00:07:26.108 --> 00:07:28.530
Have you never been in love?

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:32.754
For a moment, Vanessa's eyes went dark.

00:07:32.814 --> 00:07:34.846
Love is for idiots.

00:07:34.906 --> 00:07:37.648
She said in a low voice.

00:07:37.708 --> 00:07:46.874
Shauna touched the small diamond engagement ring on her left hand and looked out of the window, trying not to cry.

00:07:46.934 --> 00:07:50.793
She loved Graham, and he loved her.

00:07:50.853 --> 00:07:55.084
And on Christmas Eve, she was going to marry him.

00:07:55.144 --> 00:07:57.596
Don't listen to her, Shauna.

00:07:57.656 --> 00:07:59.217
Said Haminda.

00:07:59.277 --> 00:08:01.548
Shauna liked Haminda.

00:08:01.608 --> 00:08:06.090
She only looked about twenty-two, but she seemed a lot older.

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:07.513
At last.

00:08:07.573 --> 00:08:11.418
thought Shauna when she saw a sign for Dublin port.

00:08:11.478 --> 00:08:13.890
But Haminda didn't slow down.

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:17.383
She was arguing with Vanessa and she didn't see it.

00:08:17.443 --> 00:08:19.435
Haminda, the port.

00:08:19.495 --> 00:08:21.186
You've just missed the exit.

00:08:21.246 --> 00:08:22.498
Said Shauna.

00:08:22.558 --> 00:08:23.568
What?

00:08:23.628 --> 00:08:25.070
Are you sure?

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:26.180
Brilliant.

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:28.152
This is all your fault.

00:08:28.212 --> 00:08:30.334
Shouted Vanessa at Shauna.

00:08:30.394 --> 00:08:31.655
My fault.

00:08:31.715 --> 00:08:33.732
Why is it my fault?

00:08:33.792 --> 00:08:36.689
Oh, don't start all that again.

00:08:36.749 --> 00:08:41.990
I'll turn off at the next exit and we'll come back," said Huminda.

00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:46.561
But then the cars in front began to slow down and stop.

00:08:46.621 --> 00:08:51.182
That's all we need, a traffic jam, said Vanessa.

00:08:51.242 --> 00:08:54.073
We'll never get there in time now.

00:08:54.133 --> 00:08:58.764
When they eventually arrived at the ferry terminal, it was late.

00:08:58.824 --> 00:09:04.046
There were no cars or passengers waiting, only a security guard.

00:09:04.106 --> 00:09:06.889
Where do we go to get the ferry for Hollyhead?

00:09:06.949 --> 00:09:08.450
Shauna asked him.

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:17.064
The security guard pointed behind him at the ferry, which was already sailing away from the port.

00:09:17.084 --> 00:09:17.444
No!

00:09:17.504 --> 00:09:19.846
They said at the same time.

00:09:19.906 --> 00:09:23.907
The next ferry is tomorrow morning, at ten to seven.

00:09:23.967 --> 00:09:25.298
Said the guard.

00:09:25.358 --> 00:09:27.949
This is all your fault!

00:09:28.009 --> 00:09:29.610
Shouted Vanessa.

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:31.511
Oh, shut up!

00:09:31.571 --> 00:09:34.476
Shauna and Haminda shouted back.

00:09:34.536 --> 00:09:37.771
Luckily, they found a small hotel.

00:09:37.831 --> 00:09:44.496
They started to relax as they began to take their bags out of the car in the hotel garage.

00:09:44.555 --> 00:09:46.778
Don't forget your briefcase.

00:09:46.838 --> 00:09:53.942
Haminda said to Vanessa, she was pointing at a dark brown expensive leather briefcase.

00:09:54.002 --> 00:09:55.434
It's not mine.

00:09:55.494 --> 00:09:58.566
Vanessa said, pulling it from the car.

00:09:58.626 --> 00:10:00.678
It was quite heavy.

00:10:00.738 --> 00:10:03.099
Shauna, is it yours?

00:10:03.159 --> 00:10:04.267
No.

00:10:04.327 --> 00:10:08.195
And it's not mine, said Haminda.

00:10:08.255 --> 00:10:12.906
So it was already in the car when we left the airport.

00:10:12.966 --> 00:10:16.188
Somebody has obviously forgotten it.

00:10:16.248 --> 00:10:18.649
What do you think is inside?

00:10:18.709 --> 00:10:20.149
Said Vanessa.

00:10:20.209 --> 00:10:26.201
And for the first time that day, she smiled.

00:10:26.261 --> 00:10:37.069
Chapter 3 A sleepless night I want to open it, said Vanessa.

00:10:37.129 --> 00:10:40.590
But it's not ours, said Haminda.

00:10:40.650 --> 00:10:46.132
It was one o'clock in the morning and she was in bed trying to sleep.

00:10:46.192 --> 00:10:51.744
We've got to be up in less than four hours if we want to get the first ferry.

00:10:51.804 --> 00:10:55.165
So please go to sleep.

00:10:55.225 --> 00:11:01.046
Vanessa turned away from the briefcase and pulled the blanket over her head.

00:11:01.106 --> 00:11:03.257
We couldn't open it anyway.

00:11:03.317 --> 00:11:04.227
It's locked."

00:11:04.287 --> 00:11:06.608
said Shauna, getting into bed.

00:11:06.668 --> 00:11:09.450
But then she noticed Vanessa's smile.

00:11:09.510 --> 00:11:10.270
What?

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:11.991
Why are you smiling?

00:11:12.051 --> 00:11:17.314
Vanessa took a clip from her hair and held it between her fingers.

00:11:17.374 --> 00:11:19.094
That'll never work.

00:11:19.154 --> 00:11:20.666
Laughed Shauna.

00:11:20.726 --> 00:11:23.036
It always works in films.

00:11:23.096 --> 00:11:24.127
Go on then.

00:11:24.187 --> 00:11:25.208
Said Shauna.

00:11:25.268 --> 00:11:26.298
Do it.

00:11:26.358 --> 00:11:29.998
Haminda pulled the blankets over her head.

00:11:30.058 --> 00:11:35.346
Vanessa worked on one of the locks, using her clip as a key.

00:11:35.406 --> 00:11:36.507
I knew it.

00:11:36.567 --> 00:11:38.607
Said Shauna after a few minutes.

00:11:38.667 --> 00:11:40.628
I didn't think it was going to work.

00:11:40.688 --> 00:11:46.979
But before she could finish her sentence, there was a click and the lock opened.

00:11:47.039 --> 00:11:49.590
Haminda sat up in bed.

00:11:49.650 --> 00:11:52.701
This didn't seem the right thing to do.

00:11:52.761 --> 00:11:57.547
But now it was open, she wanted to know what was inside.

00:11:57.607 --> 00:12:00.924
Vanessa soon opened the other lock.

00:12:00.984 --> 00:12:04.276
Slowly, she opened the briefcase.

00:12:04.336 --> 00:12:10.522
Her eyes became big and round when she saw what was inside.

00:12:10.582 --> 00:12:14.354
Haminda watched their shocked faces.

00:12:14.414 --> 00:12:16.036
What's in it?

00:12:16.096 --> 00:12:17.276
Show me!

00:12:17.336 --> 00:12:20.209
Vanessa turned the case towards her.

00:12:20.268 --> 00:12:23.000
The briefcase was full of money.

00:12:23.060 --> 00:12:29.828
After a few moments, Haminda said, There are hundreds of thousands of euros here.

00:12:29.888 --> 00:12:32.190
She laughed nervously.

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:34.682
I've never seen so much money.

00:12:34.743 --> 00:12:37.534
There's only one thing we can do now.

00:12:37.594 --> 00:12:39.176
What are you doing?

00:12:39.236 --> 00:12:44.180
Vanessa said when she saw Haminda with her mobile phone in her hand.

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:46.792
I'm going to phone the police.

00:12:46.852 --> 00:12:48.703
You can't do that.

00:12:48.763 --> 00:12:54.294
Do you realise what a difference this money could make to our lives?

00:12:54.354 --> 00:12:56.373
But it's not ours.

00:12:56.434 --> 00:12:58.485
We don't know who it is.

00:12:58.545 --> 00:13:00.746
There's no label, no name.

00:13:00.806 --> 00:13:02.598
Tell her Shauna.

00:13:02.658 --> 00:13:07.442
Shauna, you know we have to go to the police, don't you?

00:13:07.502 --> 00:13:08.962
Said Haminda.

00:13:09.022 --> 00:13:10.654
I don't know.

00:13:10.714 --> 00:13:13.816
My fiancé and I really want a honeymoon.

00:13:13.876 --> 00:13:16.518
We could go anywhere in the world with this money.

00:13:16.578 --> 00:13:21.983
The Maldives, the Caribbean, New York, San Francisco, anywhere.

00:13:22.044 --> 00:13:25.458
At the moment, we're going to stay in my parents' caravan."

00:13:25.518 --> 00:13:29.211
Shauna looked into Haminda's eyes.

00:13:29.271 --> 00:13:32.214
We've never had a holiday together.

00:13:32.274 --> 00:13:34.466
I'm sorry, Haminda.

00:13:34.526 --> 00:13:37.548
Vanessa held Haminda's hands.

00:13:37.608 --> 00:13:44.260
Her voice was soft and kind, and Haminda remembered that she was an actress.

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:47.077
You said your dad's ill.

00:13:47.137 --> 00:13:48.667
Think about it.

00:13:48.727 --> 00:13:52.708
With this money, you could pay for the best doctors.

00:13:52.768 --> 00:13:55.569
Huminda's phone started to ring.

00:13:55.629 --> 00:13:59.880
Slowly, Huminda picked it up and answered.

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:01.551
Hello.

00:14:01.611 --> 00:14:03.362
Oh, hello, Mum.

00:14:03.422 --> 00:14:05.382
How's Dad?

00:14:05.442 --> 00:14:12.434
When the phone call finished, ten minutes later, her cheeks were wet with tears.

00:14:12.494 --> 00:14:14.324
What is it, Huminda?

00:14:14.384 --> 00:14:15.994
asked Shauna.

00:14:16.054 --> 00:14:19.536
My dad, he's got worse.

00:14:19.596 --> 00:14:22.816
They're not sure if he will survive.

00:14:22.876 --> 00:14:26.178
Vanessa closed the briefcase.

00:14:26.238 --> 00:14:29.549
Well then, you need to get there quickly.

00:14:29.609 --> 00:14:34.730
If we go to the police now, they'll ask us questions for hours.

00:14:34.790 --> 00:14:36.321
Okay.

00:14:36.381 --> 00:14:38.462
Said Hummingda quietly.

00:14:38.522 --> 00:14:40.712
Maybe not until tomorrow.

00:14:40.772 --> 00:14:42.386
Continued, Vanessa.

00:14:42.446 --> 00:14:44.339
I said, OK.

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:46.602
We won't go to the police now.

00:14:46.662 --> 00:14:51.186
But when we get to London, after I've seen my dad, then we'll go.

00:14:51.246 --> 00:14:53.078
Do you all agree?

00:14:53.138 --> 00:14:55.730
Shauna nodded reluctantly.

00:14:55.790 --> 00:15:00.604
But Vanessa only said, Let's get a few hours' sleep now.

00:15:00.664 --> 00:15:03.308
We don't want to miss the next ferry.

00:15:03.368 --> 00:15:07.670
This time, they arrived early and waited in the car.

00:15:07.730 --> 00:15:13.551
It wasn't snowing, but it was cold, and everything looked very dark.

00:15:13.611 --> 00:15:20.494
When they started to drive onto the ferry, Haminda saw the face of the driver of the car behind her.

00:15:20.554 --> 00:15:23.646
That's strange, she thought.

00:15:23.706 --> 00:15:28.718
It's still dark outside, but he's wearing sunglasses.

00:15:28.778 --> 00:15:30.378
Are you okay?

00:15:30.438 --> 00:15:31.879
asked Shauna.

00:15:31.939 --> 00:15:34.680
I'm cold, that's all.

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:42.161
Huminda answered, but she didn't seem sure of what she was saying.

00:15:42.222 --> 00:15:59.686
Chapter 4 On the Fairy It was dawn and Shauna and Huminda looked at the red and orange sky over Dublin as the fairy slowly left the port.

00:15:59.746 --> 00:16:02.647
When was the last time you saw your parents?

00:16:02.707 --> 00:16:04.854
Shauna asked Huminda.

00:16:04.914 --> 00:16:09.666
Four years ago, at my 18th birthday party.

00:16:09.726 --> 00:16:11.788
She answered sadly.

00:16:11.848 --> 00:16:13.058
Wow.

00:16:13.118 --> 00:16:15.190
That's a long time.

00:16:15.250 --> 00:16:18.542
They wanted me to marry someone else.

00:16:18.602 --> 00:16:20.824
Somebody they chose.

00:16:20.884 --> 00:16:22.596
An arranged marriage?

00:16:22.656 --> 00:16:23.567
Yes.

00:16:23.627 --> 00:16:25.238
Said Haminda.

00:16:25.298 --> 00:16:28.641
They stood in silence for a while.

00:16:28.701 --> 00:16:35.026
In Indian tradition, a marriage is more than just a woman and a man being together.

00:16:35.086 --> 00:16:38.096
It's a marriage of two families.

00:16:38.156 --> 00:16:42.869
I've always known that it was very important to my family.

00:16:42.929 --> 00:16:45.401
But then I met Declan.

00:16:45.460 --> 00:16:51.924
I was only 17, that I knew that I wanted to spend the rest of my life with him.

00:16:51.983 --> 00:16:55.506
And we saw each other in secret for months.

00:16:55.566 --> 00:17:02.180
I was too frightened to tell my family about it, because they believe in arranged marriages.

00:17:02.240 --> 00:17:13.964
But then my parents told me the big news At my 18th birthday party, they wanted to introduce me to my future husband, an Indian boy.

00:17:14.024 --> 00:17:17.444
I knew that I had to tell them the truth.

00:17:17.504 --> 00:17:19.575
I'm the only daughter.

00:17:19.635 --> 00:17:22.035
I've just got one brother.

00:17:22.095 --> 00:17:25.086
And my father was very angry.

00:17:25.146 --> 00:17:27.946
I had to choose, he told me.

00:17:28.006 --> 00:17:30.087
And I chose Declan.

00:17:30.147 --> 00:17:31.927
Are you still together?

00:17:31.987 --> 00:17:32.977
Yes.

00:17:33.037 --> 00:17:34.478
Said Haminda.

00:17:34.538 --> 00:17:37.043
And she touched her stomach.

00:17:37.103 --> 00:17:39.068
Are you pregnant?

00:17:39.128 --> 00:17:41.370
Shauna asked with a smile.

00:17:41.430 --> 00:17:42.700
Yes.

00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:45.142
I only got the news last week.

00:17:45.202 --> 00:17:46.482
She laughed.

00:17:46.542 --> 00:17:48.854
You're the only other person that knows.

00:17:48.874 --> 00:17:51.626
I haven't told Declan yet.

00:17:51.686 --> 00:17:55.567
I'm sure that when your dad knows he'll be happy too.

00:17:55.628 --> 00:17:57.679
Maybe.

00:17:57.739 --> 00:18:01.617
Three hours later they were in England.

00:18:01.677 --> 00:18:03.944
Haminda drove fast.

00:18:04.004 --> 00:18:08.595
They had to drive for another six hours before they arrived in London.

00:18:08.655 --> 00:18:14.387
After a few miles, Haminda noticed that Vanessa was looking over her shoulder.

00:18:14.447 --> 00:18:16.608
What's wrong, Vanessa?

00:18:16.668 --> 00:18:18.579
I...nothing.

00:18:18.639 --> 00:18:19.609
She said.

00:18:19.669 --> 00:18:21.840
Can't you drive faster?

00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:24.641
I'm already driving over the speed limit.

00:18:24.701 --> 00:18:25.821
Why?

00:18:25.881 --> 00:18:27.372
No reason.

00:18:27.432 --> 00:18:34.279
It's only I don't want to frighten anyone, but I think somebody is following us.

00:18:34.338 --> 00:18:36.920
There's a dark blue car behind us.

00:18:36.980 --> 00:18:40.342
It's been there since we got on the ferry at Dublin."

00:18:40.403 --> 00:18:43.124
Haminda looked into the mirror.

00:18:43.184 --> 00:18:47.737
Her heart began to beat faster when she saw the sunglasses.

00:18:47.797 --> 00:18:50.499
Suddenly they heard a horn.

00:18:50.559 --> 00:18:57.182
Haminda looked back at the road and saw that an enormous lorry was coming directly towards them.

00:18:57.242 --> 00:19:02.514
She turned the steering wheel to the right and pushed her foot down hard on the brake.

00:19:02.574 --> 00:19:04.925
But the lorry was getting nearer.

00:19:04.985 --> 00:19:07.496
The car seemed out of control.

00:19:07.556 --> 00:19:09.266
Someone screamed.

00:19:09.326 --> 00:19:12.178
But then the lorry passed by them.

00:19:12.238 --> 00:19:16.769
The car slowed down and Harmin de's body relaxed.

00:19:16.829 --> 00:19:20.250
Suddenly there was a loud noise.

00:19:20.310 --> 00:19:23.442
The three women all turned around.

00:19:23.502 --> 00:19:29.594
They saw the lorry crashing into the car that was following them.

00:19:29.654 --> 00:19:33.326
Chapter Five.

00:19:33.386 --> 00:19:36.318
The Road to London.

00:19:36.378 --> 00:19:40.612
They drove the rest of the journey in silence.

00:19:40.672 --> 00:19:46.125
Three hours later, when they stopped to get petrol, they were still nervous.

00:19:46.186 --> 00:19:48.337
I need to get some air.

00:19:48.398 --> 00:19:51.050
Vanessa said, getting out of the car.

00:19:51.110 --> 00:19:53.001
Are you coming too, Shauna?

00:19:53.061 --> 00:19:55.172
Shauna shook her head.

00:19:55.232 --> 00:19:58.966
Vanessa didn't want to go anywhere by herself.

00:19:59.026 --> 00:20:00.887
She turned to Arminda.

00:20:00.947 --> 00:20:02.298
"'What about you?'

00:20:02.358 --> 00:20:03.678
she asked.

00:20:03.738 --> 00:20:09.122
"'I want to leave as soon as I filled the car up with petrol,' said Arminda.

00:20:09.183 --> 00:20:15.228
Vanessa felt stupid for being so nervous, but she couldn't stop herself.

00:20:15.288 --> 00:20:19.851
In the toilets she looked at herself in the mirror and laughed.

00:20:19.911 --> 00:20:22.132
She looked terrible.

00:20:22.192 --> 00:20:25.956
Without makeup she looked older than thirty-five.

00:20:26.016 --> 00:20:28.257
But she was alive.

00:20:28.317 --> 00:20:38.004
When Ben left her for her best friend, she was only 25, with the lead role in a musical that was going to take her all over the world.

00:20:38.064 --> 00:20:44.770
But she gave it all up, because she loved him, and she didn't want to be away from him.

00:20:44.830 --> 00:20:48.034
In the end, he left her anyway.

00:20:48.094 --> 00:20:57.570
There were other boyfriends, but for the last 10 years, she never really loved anyone else, because she never wanted to be hurt again.

00:20:57.630 --> 00:21:02.961
She was never afraid of anything, because there was nothing left to lose.

00:21:03.021 --> 00:21:04.931
Until today.

00:21:04.991 --> 00:21:09.492
Now, after the crash, things were different.

00:21:09.552 --> 00:21:12.172
Vanessa wanted to live.

00:21:12.232 --> 00:21:14.763
She wanted to change.

00:21:14.823 --> 00:21:17.854
Why didn't she listen to Arminda?

00:21:17.914 --> 00:21:21.054
Why didn't they go to the police before?

00:21:21.114 --> 00:21:23.994
Now, it was too late.

00:21:24.054 --> 00:21:27.281
Why did she never listen?

00:21:27.341 --> 00:21:31.318
She went inside and ordered a cup of coffee.

00:21:31.378 --> 00:21:34.999
The person behind the bar was reading a newspaper.

00:21:35.059 --> 00:21:39.760
Vanessa saw the date, the 22nd of December.

00:21:39.820 --> 00:21:42.671
They only left Galway yesterday.

00:21:42.731 --> 00:21:45.162
It seemed a lot longer.

00:21:45.222 --> 00:21:49.312
There was a small television on the wall over the bar.

00:21:49.373 --> 00:21:51.636
The news was on.

00:21:51.696 --> 00:21:58.351
A body was found in the car park of Galway Airport, Ireland, in the early hours of this morning.

00:21:58.411 --> 00:22:05.193
A 33-year-old Colin O'Flahity, manager of a car hire at Galway Airport, was shot in the chest.

00:22:05.253 --> 00:22:09.074
The police believed the killing was related to drug trafficking.

00:22:09.134 --> 00:22:11.235
It's terrible, isn't it?

00:22:11.295 --> 00:22:15.076
Said the barman, passing Vanessa her glass of water.

00:22:15.136 --> 00:22:18.938
Vanessa realized that she was staring at the television.

00:22:18.998 --> 00:22:20.994
Her face was white.

00:22:21.054 --> 00:22:23.092
Her mouth opened.

00:22:23.152 --> 00:22:25.203
It's in the newspapers.

00:22:25.263 --> 00:22:26.434
Look.

00:22:26.494 --> 00:22:28.956
He passed her the newspaper.

00:22:29.016 --> 00:22:33.569
Family man killed in drug shooting, said the headline.

00:22:33.630 --> 00:22:40.334
In the centre of the page, there was a photo of Colin O'Flahati on holiday with his three-year-old son.

00:22:40.394 --> 00:22:45.858
They were obviously on a boat, and Colin was holding a very big fish.

00:22:45.918 --> 00:22:48.601
They looked so happy.

00:22:48.661 --> 00:22:51.595
Vanessa felt sick.

00:22:51.655 --> 00:22:54.058
She looked back at the television.

00:22:54.118 --> 00:22:56.368
A young woman was crying.

00:22:56.428 --> 00:23:05.791
At the bottom of the screen, Vanessa read, Mrs. Moira O'Flahity, Mr. O'Flahity's wife.

00:23:05.851 --> 00:23:13.313
If anyone knows anything, anything at all, please, for my little boy, please contact the police.

00:23:13.373 --> 00:23:16.934
Her voice sounded more and more desperate.

00:23:16.994 --> 00:23:21.399
Vanessa felt like the woman was talking directly to her.

00:23:21.459 --> 00:23:24.374
Anything at all, please?"

00:23:24.434 --> 00:23:26.875
Vanessa couldn't hear any more.

00:23:26.934 --> 00:23:33.486
She ran from the bar, still holding the newspaper in her left hand.

00:23:33.547 --> 00:23:39.008
Chapter 6 Act the Hospital.

00:23:39.028 --> 00:23:42.160
"'Go on.

00:23:42.220 --> 00:23:44.650
We'll wait here for you,' said Shauna.

00:23:44.670 --> 00:23:47.520
"'But what if they come back?'

00:23:47.580 --> 00:23:49.620
You saw that accident.

00:23:49.680 --> 00:23:52.102
We'll be all right for a couple of hours.

00:23:52.162 --> 00:23:53.883
Insisted Vanessa.

00:23:53.943 --> 00:23:57.085
Huminda looked nervously at the hospital.

00:23:57.145 --> 00:24:00.837
She took a deep breath and got out of the car.

00:24:00.898 --> 00:24:03.219
I'll be as quick as I can.

00:24:03.279 --> 00:24:06.281
But this is my mobile number if you need me.

00:24:06.341 --> 00:24:10.034
She quickly wrote it down and gave it to Shauna.

00:24:10.094 --> 00:24:14.569
Inside the hospital, Huminda took the lift to the ninth floor.

00:24:14.629 --> 00:24:18.794
When the doors opened, her little brother was waiting for her.

00:24:18.855 --> 00:24:21.566
But he wasn't so little anymore.

00:24:21.626 --> 00:24:26.640
The last time she saw him, he was nine years old, a child.

00:24:26.701 --> 00:24:31.854
Now he was thirteen, and he was a lot taller than Haminda.

00:24:31.914 --> 00:24:38.188
There were so many things she wanted to ask him, but she could only say his name.

00:24:38.248 --> 00:24:39.839
Perindra!

00:24:39.900 --> 00:24:41.922
What is she doing here?

00:24:41.982 --> 00:24:44.715
Her father's voice interrupted them.

00:24:44.775 --> 00:24:49.350
He was seriously ill, but his voice was still strong.

00:24:49.410 --> 00:24:52.973
Meena, did you ask her to come here?

00:24:53.033 --> 00:24:58.688
Meena, Haminda's mother, looked elegant in a red silk sari.

00:24:58.748 --> 00:25:03.822
When she saw her daughter, there were tears of happiness in her eyes.

00:25:03.882 --> 00:25:08.695
Dad, oh Dad, I've missed you so much.

00:25:08.755 --> 00:25:11.146
Haminda ran towards him.

00:25:11.206 --> 00:25:13.308
His face was grey.

00:25:13.368 --> 00:25:18.422
His hair was thinner than she remembered, and he looked old and weak.

00:25:18.482 --> 00:25:23.366
But his eyes were angry, just like they were four years ago.

00:25:23.426 --> 00:25:25.388
I don't want you here.

00:25:25.448 --> 00:25:27.490
You made your decision.

00:25:27.550 --> 00:25:29.230
Please leave.

00:25:29.290 --> 00:25:36.416
Haminda touched his hand, but he closed his eyes and turned away from her.

00:25:36.476 --> 00:25:38.942
But I've come from Ireland.

00:25:39.002 --> 00:25:41.528
Dad, please listen to me!

00:25:41.588 --> 00:25:42.568
Dad!"

00:25:42.628 --> 00:25:49.651
she shouted as they took him into the operating room on a trolley, Mina and Perindra next to him.

00:25:49.711 --> 00:25:51.532
I love you, Dad.

00:25:51.592 --> 00:25:52.542
She said.

00:25:52.602 --> 00:25:54.493
But he was gone.

00:25:54.553 --> 00:25:58.654
She was alone in the long white corridor.

00:25:58.714 --> 00:26:03.946
She sat down, put her head in her hands, and cried.

00:26:04.006 --> 00:26:08.318
All her hopes of a happy reunion were gone.

00:26:08.378 --> 00:26:11.830
It was not going to be easy for him to meet her again.

00:26:11.890 --> 00:26:13.651
Haminda knew that.

00:26:13.711 --> 00:26:17.214
But she didn't think it was going to be this difficult.

00:26:17.274 --> 00:26:21.906
Why didn't he understand that she never wanted to choose?

00:26:21.966 --> 00:26:27.930
Why couldn't he see that she was still his daughter, still his little girl?

00:26:27.990 --> 00:26:35.194
Why couldn't he see that she still needed her dad, even if she loved Declan?

00:26:35.254 --> 00:26:43.644
When she couldn't cry anymore, She stood up and decided to go with Shauna and Vanessa to the police station.

00:26:43.704 --> 00:26:49.789
Later on I'll come back and I won't leave until he understands.

00:26:49.849 --> 00:26:52.480
She thought as she went outside.

00:26:52.540 --> 00:27:04.380
When she got to the car park the car was there but there was no Shauna and Vanessa and there was no briefcase full of money.

00:27:04.440 --> 00:27:10.948
Chapter 7 Danger money.

00:27:11.009 --> 00:27:15.460
Shauna and Vanessa were in the back of the car.

00:27:15.520 --> 00:27:17.370
Their hands were tied.

00:27:17.430 --> 00:27:23.632
They were very frightened as they tried to listen to the conversation of the two men in front of them.

00:27:23.692 --> 00:27:28.063
What are you going to do with your 10% of the money, Steve?

00:27:28.123 --> 00:27:30.634
I'd like to go on a nice holiday.

00:27:30.694 --> 00:27:32.224
Somewhere out.

00:27:32.284 --> 00:27:34.035
What about you?

00:27:34.095 --> 00:27:36.826
Vanessa looked at the two men.

00:27:36.886 --> 00:27:38.588
She had to concentrate.

00:27:38.648 --> 00:27:43.133
She had to think of a plan, and she needed to think quickly.

00:27:43.193 --> 00:27:45.685
But she could only think of one thing.

00:27:45.745 --> 00:27:49.158
Colin O'Flahat is three-year-old son.

00:27:49.218 --> 00:27:55.072
While they were waiting for her men to outside the hospital, these two men came up to them.

00:27:55.132 --> 00:28:00.385
They were smiling and seemed nice when they asked for directions to King's Cross Station.

00:28:00.445 --> 00:28:06.580
But when Shauna was pointing the best way to them, the two men pushed them both into their car.

00:28:06.640 --> 00:28:09.489
They wanted the briefcase.

00:28:09.549 --> 00:28:15.140
Did you see that crash between the lorry and the car with the plainclothes police?

00:28:15.200 --> 00:28:16.872
Laugh Steve.

00:28:16.933 --> 00:28:22.316
He saw the wave and Essa and Shawna looked at each other, suddenly realising the truth.

00:28:22.376 --> 00:28:24.668
Did you think that was us?

00:28:24.728 --> 00:28:26.590
Laugh the driver.

00:28:26.650 --> 00:28:30.222
They thought that was us in that accident.

00:28:30.282 --> 00:28:33.525
And they laughed even louder.

00:28:33.585 --> 00:28:36.047
Just then, their telephone rang.

00:28:36.107 --> 00:28:38.478
The driver answered the call.

00:28:38.538 --> 00:28:40.238
Yes boss.

00:28:40.298 --> 00:28:41.798
Okay.

00:28:41.858 --> 00:28:44.298
The old building in East London.

00:28:44.358 --> 00:28:46.679
Of course we've got the money.

00:28:46.739 --> 00:28:48.690
We're not stupid.

00:28:48.750 --> 00:28:51.000
And the two ladies.

00:28:51.060 --> 00:28:52.451
No.

00:28:52.511 --> 00:28:54.362
There were only two.

00:28:54.422 --> 00:28:56.872
What do you mean there's another one?

00:28:56.932 --> 00:28:59.364
You'll have to go and get her.

00:28:59.424 --> 00:29:03.105
Vanessa knew then what she had to do.

00:29:03.165 --> 00:29:10.036
Carefully, she pulled her mobile phone from her coat pocket and started to write a text message.

00:29:10.096 --> 00:29:13.336
You are in danger.

00:29:13.396 --> 00:29:18.922
Men taking us to building in East London.

00:29:18.982 --> 00:29:20.804
Be careful.

00:29:20.864 --> 00:29:24.056
Men coming for you.

00:29:24.116 --> 00:29:26.760
Go to police.

00:29:26.820 --> 00:29:29.542
S and V.

00:29:29.602 --> 00:29:33.784
It seemed to take forever to write the short message.

00:29:33.844 --> 00:29:42.605
She took out the piece of paper with Haminda's number on it and typed 354-781-2330.

00:29:42.665 --> 00:29:48.618
Now, she only needed to press send and then Haminda could get help.

00:29:48.678 --> 00:29:49.808
Hey!

00:29:49.868 --> 00:29:51.238
What are you doing?

00:29:51.298 --> 00:29:52.739
Give me that!

00:29:52.799 --> 00:29:56.020
Steve turned around and tried to grab the phone.

00:29:56.080 --> 00:30:01.456
Vanessa tried to press send, but he was pulling the phone out of her hand.

00:30:01.516 --> 00:30:03.251
Leave her alone!"

00:30:03.311 --> 00:30:07.963
shouted Shorna, pulling on his arm, trying to free Vanessa.

00:30:08.023 --> 00:30:12.316
The driver was looking at them and couldn't control the car anymore.

00:30:12.376 --> 00:30:16.458
Steve got out his gun, but Shorna pushed him and he dropped it.

00:30:16.478 --> 00:30:19.269
"'You stupid woman!"

00:30:19.329 --> 00:30:23.151
he shouted as he looked desperately around his feet for it.

00:30:23.211 --> 00:30:26.792
Just then a police siren sounded in the distance.

00:30:26.852 --> 00:30:31.394
Steve looked up and saw that the police car was blocking the road in front of them.

00:30:31.454 --> 00:30:34.656
Its blue light was bright in the dark evening.

00:30:34.716 --> 00:30:38.148
The driver pushed his foot down hard on the brake.

00:30:38.208 --> 00:30:42.740
Shauna realized with horror that they were going straight for it.

00:30:42.800 --> 00:30:44.461
Too fast!

00:30:44.521 --> 00:30:49.404
The car began to move from side to side, dangerously out of control.

00:30:49.464 --> 00:30:51.245
Vanessa screamed.

00:30:51.305 --> 00:30:54.607
Shauna held her breath, ready for the crash.

00:30:54.667 --> 00:30:57.509
She closed her eyes, waiting.

00:30:57.569 --> 00:31:01.012
Her body went quickly forwards, and then back.

00:31:01.072 --> 00:31:03.194
But there was no crash.

00:31:03.254 --> 00:31:08.808
When she was sure that the car wasn't moving anymore, she slowly opened her eyes.

00:31:08.868 --> 00:31:12.492
The car was just a few centimeters from a police car.

00:31:12.552 --> 00:31:19.268
Suddenly, a lot of policemen were all around the car, and Shauna could finally breathe.

00:31:19.328 --> 00:31:24.158
Their nightmare was over.

00:31:24.218 --> 00:31:31.598
Chapter eight, Haminda alone.

00:31:31.658 --> 00:31:35.612
I'm sure they think I'm really stupid.

00:31:35.672 --> 00:31:37.222
Thought Haminda.

00:31:37.282 --> 00:31:41.246
And I am, because I believed them.

00:31:41.306 --> 00:31:46.248
Spend time with your dad before his operation, they said.

00:31:46.308 --> 00:31:50.471
They weren't worried about me spending time with Dad.

00:31:50.532 --> 00:31:55.319
The only thing they wanted was enough time to escape with the money.

00:31:55.379 --> 00:31:58.334
Vanessa didn't want to go to the police.

00:31:58.394 --> 00:32:00.444
She said that very clearly.

00:32:00.504 --> 00:32:01.905
But Shauna.

00:32:01.965 --> 00:32:03.756
Shauna was different.

00:32:03.816 --> 00:32:07.977
At least, Hummingda thought Shauna was different.

00:32:08.037 --> 00:32:12.358
She thought that after all this was over, they could be friends.

00:32:12.418 --> 00:32:16.720
But now, she didn't know what to think anymore.

00:32:16.780 --> 00:32:20.651
Maybe they've gone to get a drink or something to eat.

00:32:20.711 --> 00:32:22.102
Thought Hummingda.

00:32:22.162 --> 00:32:24.444
But she knew the truth.

00:32:24.504 --> 00:32:33.058
Without Huminda there to stop her, Vanessa probably talked to Shauna about all the places Shauna could go on her honeymoon.

00:32:33.118 --> 00:32:34.979
They could share the money.

00:32:35.039 --> 00:32:36.239
Half each.

00:32:36.299 --> 00:32:37.779
Fifty-fifty.

00:32:37.839 --> 00:32:41.710
That was enough to go on honeymoon for over three months.

00:32:41.770 --> 00:32:44.451
Huminda could hear Vanessa.

00:32:44.511 --> 00:32:47.212
It was so easy to believe her.

00:32:47.272 --> 00:32:50.382
She was the perfect actress.

00:32:50.442 --> 00:32:52.138
Excuse me.

00:32:52.198 --> 00:32:55.865
said her gentle voice, making Harmina jump.

00:32:55.925 --> 00:32:58.858
Sorry, I didn't want to frighten you.

00:32:58.918 --> 00:33:02.630
Harmina turned around and saw a young man.

00:33:02.691 --> 00:33:10.326
He was smiling kindly, and when Harmina saw that his arm was in a plaster, she started to relax.

00:33:10.386 --> 00:33:12.458
No, I'm sorry.

00:33:12.519 --> 00:33:14.260
How can I help?

00:33:14.320 --> 00:33:17.491
Can you tell me the way to Kings Cross station?

00:33:17.551 --> 00:33:24.761
I came here in an ambulance, but I don't know this part of London, and I'm not sure how to get back home from here.

00:33:24.821 --> 00:33:30.552
I don't know, but I've got a map in the car, said Haminda.

00:33:30.612 --> 00:33:35.753
She was about to put the key in the door when her mobile phone beeped.

00:33:35.813 --> 00:33:37.854
She had a new message.

00:33:37.914 --> 00:33:46.215
She took the phone out of her pocket and began to read, you are in danger.

00:33:46.275 --> 00:33:49.906
No, this can't be happening.

00:33:49.966 --> 00:33:54.277
These things happen in films, not to people like me."

00:33:54.337 --> 00:33:58.028
She thought, reading the message a second time.

00:33:58.088 --> 00:34:02.499
She looked up slowly at the reflection of the man in the car window.

00:34:02.559 --> 00:34:06.250
For a moment, she couldn't believe what she saw.

00:34:06.310 --> 00:34:09.200
She was too frightened to breathe.

00:34:09.260 --> 00:34:11.911
He was taking off the plaster.

00:34:11.971 --> 00:34:13.512
It was fake.

00:34:13.572 --> 00:34:16.175
He didn't have a broken arm.

00:34:16.235 --> 00:34:19.880
He was taking something out of his jacket.

00:34:19.940 --> 00:34:23.332
Then Haminda realized what it was.

00:34:23.392 --> 00:34:27.664
He was pulling out a gun.

00:34:27.725 --> 00:34:38.481
Chapter 9 Back Together Just a minute, said Haminda.

00:34:38.541 --> 00:34:42.554
She looked around, careful not to alarm the gunman.

00:34:42.614 --> 00:34:45.431
But the car park was dark and empty.

00:34:45.491 --> 00:34:47.948
There was nobody to ask for help.

00:34:48.008 --> 00:34:52.220
In the glass of the car window, she saw him raise the gun.

00:34:52.280 --> 00:34:57.012
Without thinking, she turned around and surprised him with a powerful kick.

00:34:57.072 --> 00:34:58.723
The man fell back.

00:34:58.783 --> 00:35:02.214
The gun dropped to the floor and went under the car.

00:35:02.274 --> 00:35:06.386
His head hit the side of the car and he fell to the ground.

00:35:06.446 --> 00:35:09.298
Harmina didn't wait for him to wake up.

00:35:09.358 --> 00:35:13.824
She quickly died the number of the emergency services, 999.

00:35:13.884 --> 00:35:18.391
Every second seemed like a year as she listened to the ringing.

00:35:18.451 --> 00:35:20.852
Then a woman's voice answered.

00:35:20.912 --> 00:35:22.662
Emergency services?

00:35:22.722 --> 00:35:24.443
Which service do you require?

00:35:24.503 --> 00:35:26.574
Police, ambulance or fire?

00:35:26.634 --> 00:35:29.284
And Haminda started to cry.

00:35:29.344 --> 00:35:31.365
Police, please.

00:35:31.425 --> 00:35:32.576
Hello.

00:35:32.636 --> 00:35:33.906
Police.

00:35:33.966 --> 00:35:35.686
There's a man with a gun.

00:35:35.746 --> 00:35:37.257
He wants to shoot me.

00:35:37.317 --> 00:35:40.790
I'm outside the Queen Elizabeth Hospital in London.

00:35:40.850 --> 00:35:51.668
But before she could finish telling the operator everything, there was a loud bang, pain, and then for Haminda, everything went black.

00:35:51.728 --> 00:36:02.056
Haminda could see lights, bright white lights, and her first thought was that she was dead.

00:36:02.116 --> 00:36:09.444
But then she felt someone touch her hand, and her mother's sweet voice said her name.

00:36:09.504 --> 00:36:17.793
Slowly, Huminda opened her eyes and her mother's face slowly became clear.

00:36:17.853 --> 00:36:22.998
Mom, it's all right, my darling.

00:36:23.058 --> 00:36:25.340
What happened?

00:36:25.400 --> 00:36:27.150
Where am I?

00:36:27.210 --> 00:36:30.563
You were shot, but you're going to be fine.

00:36:30.624 --> 00:36:32.666
You're in hospital.

00:36:32.726 --> 00:36:35.328
What about my baby?

00:36:35.388 --> 00:36:38.782
Huminda started to feel frightened.

00:36:38.842 --> 00:36:41.366
Your baby's fine.

00:36:41.426 --> 00:36:48.580
Harmina saw that there were tears in her mother's eyes, but they were tears of happiness.

00:36:48.640 --> 00:36:51.822
I'm going to be a grandmother.

00:36:51.882 --> 00:36:55.206
Harmina looked around the room.

00:36:55.266 --> 00:36:57.256
Perindra was there.

00:36:57.316 --> 00:37:00.228
Even Shauna and Vanessa were there.

00:37:00.288 --> 00:37:04.792
Everyone except her dad and Declan.

00:37:04.852 --> 00:37:07.116
Where were they?

00:37:07.176 --> 00:37:09.219
What day is it?

00:37:09.279 --> 00:37:10.740
asked Haminda.

00:37:10.800 --> 00:37:12.782
It's Christmas Eve.

00:37:12.842 --> 00:37:15.063
You're getting married.

00:37:15.124 --> 00:37:18.315
And what about your audition, Vanessa?

00:37:18.376 --> 00:37:20.377
I got the part, of course.

00:37:20.437 --> 00:37:23.610
It's a thriller about some dangerous criminals.

00:37:23.670 --> 00:37:26.832
We're starting filming next week in France.

00:37:26.892 --> 00:37:28.994
And I'm getting married in?

00:37:29.054 --> 00:37:31.766
Shauna looked excitedly at the clock.

00:37:31.826 --> 00:37:34.043
About three hours from now.

00:37:34.103 --> 00:37:35.889
I really must go now.

00:37:35.949 --> 00:37:38.330
My mum is waiting for me with my dress.

00:37:38.390 --> 00:37:40.901
But I just wanted to see you before.

00:37:40.961 --> 00:37:43.512
We wanted to know that you were okay."

00:37:43.572 --> 00:37:45.092
smiled Vanessa.

00:37:45.152 --> 00:37:52.614
There was only one more thing Harmina wanted to know, but she was also afraid of hearing the answer.

00:37:52.674 --> 00:37:56.845
Mum, how did Dad's operation go?

00:37:56.905 --> 00:37:58.596
Harmina asked.

00:37:58.656 --> 00:38:03.654
But before Mina could answer, the door to Harmina's room opened.

00:38:03.714 --> 00:38:07.993
I hope this young man drives his car better than he does a wheelchair.

00:38:08.053 --> 00:38:09.804
Said Haminda's father.

00:38:09.864 --> 00:38:14.826
Declan pushed him into the room and next to Haminda's bed.

00:38:14.886 --> 00:38:16.966
I love you.

00:38:17.026 --> 00:38:21.398
Declan whispered and kissed her gently on the lips.

00:38:21.458 --> 00:38:25.320
Then Haminda's father took her hand.

00:38:25.380 --> 00:38:34.784
Haminda, when I heard you were shocked and in danger of dying, I thought about all those years.

00:38:34.844 --> 00:38:39.074
I realized that what is important is that you're happy.

00:38:39.134 --> 00:38:41.115
And if it is Declan?

00:38:41.175 --> 00:38:43.696
He reached up for Declan's hand.

00:38:43.756 --> 00:38:45.336
That makes you happy.

00:38:45.396 --> 00:38:47.586
Then I am happy.

00:38:47.647 --> 00:38:51.927
Seeing her tears, he looked suddenly worried.

00:38:51.987 --> 00:38:54.358
You are happy, aren't you?

00:38:54.418 --> 00:38:58.038
Yes, she said quietly.

00:38:58.098 --> 00:39:00.034
I am now.

00:39:00.094 --> 00:39:02.950
Now that my family is back together.

